dium to that date, with space for over 100,000 spectators. The 1932 Olympics were hampered by the long and difficult travel for many countries to get their teams to the West Coast of the United States. Coupled with the severe world-wide economic depression, it caused attendance to be down somewhat from the last two Olympics. Average crowds for track &amp; field still topped 60,000 people, with one day having 86,443 spectators."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The heroine of the athletics competition was " [:a {:href "/athletes/77808"} "Babe Didrikson"] ", who won the " [:a {:href "/results/58121"} "80 metre hurdles"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/58142"} "javelin throw"] ", and placed second in the " [:a {:href "/results/58128"} "high jump"] ". She would later become a professional golfer and, for a time, was the top female golfer in the world. She is often considered the greatest all-around female athlete of all time. Women competed in six events in 1932, up one from " [:a {:href "/editions/9/sports/ATH"} "Amsterdam"] ", with the 80 metre hurdles and javelin throw added, but the 800 metres was off the programme. On the men’s side, " [:a {:href "/athletes/79132"} "Eddie Tolan"] " won both sprint races, defeating his arch-rival " [:a {:href "/athletes/78787"} "Ralph Metcalfe"] "."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/57919"} "100 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "31 July –  1 August 1932"] "\n" [:td {} "33"] "\n" [:td {} "17"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/57937"} "200 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "2 –  3 August 1932"] "\n" [:td {} "25"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/57955"} "400 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td